                            <comment id="335561" author="adilger" created="Fri, 20 May 2022 07:43:10 +0000">&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;# mount.lustre /dev/mapper/mds1_flakey /mnt/lustre-mds1 -o rdonly_dev
mount.lustre: mount /dev/mapper/mds1_flakey at /mnt/lustre-mds1 failed: Operation not supported
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The reason this returns "Operation not supported" is because this feature was removed from the code (it used to be implemented as a kernel patch), and replaced by "dm-flakey" to allow discarding writes to the filesystem.  I don't think that should relate to implementing "-o ro" at all.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
